{{!--
  The Overview tab (D-687, laid out as WoW's own paper doll by D-689): the
  figure of every slot with what is worn or held in it, and a column beside
  it saying what all of it is doing.

  Spans the Skills column (D11 SS1), like Gear, Progress and Spells.

  **Twenty sockets, eighteen keys**: eight down the left, eight down the
  right, four hands beneath, and the Finger and Trinket slots draw two each.
  The three rosters come from `rules/worn.mjs` and are ITERATED - a list
  retyped here would be a second roster to keep in step.

  **EACH SOCKET IS A SQUARE ICON AND NOTHING ELSE** (the lead's reference,
  2026-09-20). D-689's plates printed the slot's label and the thing's name
  and the right column's were MIRRORED so both columns' words faced the
  portrait; a socket has no words to turn round, and the columns simply flank
  the figure the way WoW's character pane does.

  **Every tile carries `data-slot`, and that is its drop zone.** The sheet's
  `dropZoneOf` answers BY KIND - `[data-slot]` here, `[data-container-id]` on
  the Gear tab - so a ring dropped on a Finger tile is worn rather than
  falling into the container path as a move to nowhere.

  **An empty tile says *Empty* in words** (D5, CLAUDE.md SS22): an unfilled box
  is a colour, and colour is never the only carrier. Since the sockets became
  icon-only (the lead, 2026-09-20) those words live in each tile's
  `aria-label` and in its tooltip; the figure carries the
  `data-tooltip-class` both read, because core takes it off the nearest
  ancestor that has one.
--}}
<section class="tab azeroth-panel azeroth-panel-wide {{tab.cssClass}}" data-tab="overview" data-group="primary">

  <div class="azeroth-overview">

    <div class="azeroth-overview-figure" data-tooltip-class="azeroth azeroth-item-tip">
      <h3 class="azeroth-panel-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.Worn"}}</h3>
      {{#if overview.nothing}}
      <p class="azeroth-note">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.NothingWorn"}}</p>
      {{/if}}

      <div class="azeroth-doll">
        <div class="azeroth-doll-column">
          {{#each overview.left as |tile|}}
          {{> systems/azeroth-rpg/templates/actor/partials/slot-tile.hbs tile=tile}}
          {{/each}}
        </div>

        {{!-- The portrait between the columns. `alt` is empty: the name is on
              the banner two inches above it and a repeat is noise to a reader
              on a screen reader.

              **THIS IS THE CHARACTER ART** (`system.art`, D-700), not the
              token and not the directory portrait: the lead asked for *the
              Character art shown between the gear tabs on Overview* and for a
              way to set it from here. The image IS the control that sets it -
              `editArt` opens a FilePicker and writes `system.art` - and it
              falls back to `actor.img` while nothing is set, so the tab reads
              as it always did on a character made before the field.

              **The View button is a SECOND control with a second job**, drawn
              only where art is set. The NPC banner's portrait opens the art
              because that portrait is the TOKEN and the art is a different
              image; here the portrait already IS the art, so clicking it to
              see a larger copy of itself is the weaker gesture and setting it
              is the ask. Two controls, both labelled, neither hidden. --}}
        {{!-- `is-empty` where NOTHING has been set (D-700's `hasArt` reads the
              stored field, never the resolved one). The fallback is core's
              mystery-man, a white silhouette on nothing, and at the size the
              figure grew to (the lead, 2026-09-20) it was the brightest thing
              on the tab. The class is what lets the frame read as an EMPTY
              FRAME rather than as a picture of somebody. --}}
        <div class="azeroth-doll-portrait{{#unless overview.hasArt}} is-empty{{/unless}}">
          <img src="{{overview.portrait}}" alt=""
               {{#if editable}}data-action="editArt" data-tooltip="{{localize 'AZEROTH.Overview.SetArt'}}"{{/if}}>
          {{#if overview.hasArt}}
          <button type="button" class="azeroth-doll-art-view" data-action="viewArt"
                  data-tooltip="{{localize 'AZEROTH.Sheet.ViewArt'}}">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.ViewArt"}}</button>
          {{/if}}
        </div>

        {{!-- The right column takes the same socket as the left; only the
              roster differs (`FIGURE_RIGHT`). --}}
        <div class="azeroth-doll-column">
          {{#each overview.right as |tile|}}
          {{> systems/azeroth-rpg/templates/actor/partials/slot-tile.hbs tile=tile}}
          {{/each}}
        </div>
      </div>

      {{!-- The hands row is centred under the figure, so its heading is too:
            left-aligned it read as an orphan at the foot of the left socket
            column (the preview, 2026-09-20). --}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading azeroth-doll-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.Hands"}}</h4>
      <div class="azeroth-doll-hands">
        {{#each overview.hands as |tile|}}
        {{> systems/azeroth-rpg/templates/actor/partials/slot-tile.hbs tile=tile}}
        {{/each}}
      </div>

      {{#if overview.barredNote}}
      {{!-- WHY THE OFF HAND IS SHUT, IN WORDS (D-689). The socket is greyed
            and carries no action; an icon-only tile has nowhere to say why,
            and a tooltip nobody hovers is not a refusal - so the sentence is
            printed here, under the row the socket is in. --}}
      <p class="azeroth-doll-barred">{{overview.barredNote}}</p>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if overview.alsoReady}}
      {{!-- 06 SS2 owns the hands and nothing in the book says a shield puts a
            blade down, so a second equipped weapon is LISTED rather than
            taken away (D-687). --}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.AlsoReady"}}</h4>
      <ul class="azeroth-overview-ready">
        {{#each overview.alsoReady as |row|}}
        <li data-item-id="{{row.id}}">
          {{> systems/azeroth-rpg/templates/actor/partials/item-icon.hbs img=row.img rarityClass=row.rarityClass}}
          <span class="azeroth-overview-ready-name{{#if row.rarityClass}} {{row.rarityClass}}{{/if}}"
                data-action="openItem" role="button" tabindex="0">{{row.name}}</span>
        </li>
        {{/each}}
      </ul>
      {{/if}}

      {{!-- WHAT IS ACTING ON THE CHARACTER RIGHT NOW (the lead, 2026-09-20),
            in the band of slab the figure leaves under the hands row - the
            portrait is width-bound at 3:4 and cannot fill the height without
            cropping, so that band was empty.

            **ALWAYS DRAWN**, so the panel keeps its height and the tab does
            not jump as a fight starts and stops, and so the line that says
            there is nothing stands where the rows would be - the rule
            `effect-list.hbs` keeps on Core with `always` (D-665). --}}
      {{> systems/azeroth-rpg/templates/actor/partials/in-play.hbs inPlay=overview.inPlay}}
    </div>

    {{!-- What all of it is doing, on one screen. Every number here is derived
          in `prepareDerivedData`; nothing on this list is stored. --}}
    <div class="azeroth-overview-force">
      {{!-- **STATS**, and it was *In force* until the lead read it (2026-09-20:
            *Rephrase 'in force'. Idk what that means*). The pane says what the
            gear and the effects give you, every plate under it names its own
            section, and Stats is the game's own word for that. The two
            ordinary English sentences elsewhere - *No effects in force.* on
            Core and the Corruption note - are left alone. --}}
      <h3 class="azeroth-panel-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.Stats"}}</h3>

      {{#if overview.inForce.shape}}
      {{!-- THE SHAPE WORN (02 §7, D-769), first: every number under it that
            the block gives moved with it, and the line says whose they are. --}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Shape.Heading"}}</h4>
      <p class="azeroth-force-line">{{overview.inForce.shape.line}}
        <span class="azeroth-force-from">{{overview.inForce.shape.from}}</span></p>
      {{#if overview.inForce.shape.ward}}<p class="azeroth-force-line">{{overview.inForce.shape.ward}}</p>{{/if}}
      {{#if overview.inForce.shape.melded}}<p class="azeroth-force-line azeroth-force-from">{{overview.inForce.shape.melded}}</p>{{/if}}
      {{/if}}

      {{#if overview.inForce.abilities}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.Attributes"}}</h4>
      <dl class="azeroth-force-list">
        {{#each overview.inForce.abilities as |row|}}
        <dt>{{localize row.label}}</dt>
        <dd><span class="azeroth-force-value">+{{row.points}}</span> <span class="azeroth-force-from">{{row.from}}</span></dd>
        {{/each}}
      </dl>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if overview.inForce.ward}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.Ward"}}</h4>
      <dl class="azeroth-force-list">
        {{#each overview.inForce.ward as |row|}}
        <dt>{{localize row.label}}</dt>
        <dd><span class="azeroth-force-value">{{row.value}}</span></dd>
        {{/each}}
      </dl>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if overview.inForce.spellpower}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.Spellpower"}}</h4>
      <dl class="azeroth-force-list">
        {{#each overview.inForce.spellpower as |row|}}
        <dt>{{localize row.label}}</dt>
        <dd><span class="azeroth-force-value">+{{row.value}}</span></dd>
        {{/each}}
      </dl>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if overview.inForce.boons}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.Boons"}}</h4>
      <dl class="azeroth-force-list">
        {{#each overview.inForce.boons as |row|}}
        <dt>{{localize row.label}}</dt>
        <dd><span class="azeroth-force-from">{{row.from}}</span></dd>
        {{/each}}
      </dl>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if overview.inForce.scalars}}
      {{!-- What a worn thing adds to a number this column already prints
            (08 SS20): Defense, the Attack Test, Speed, Initiative. The heading
            below gives the TOTAL Defense, so this row is what moved it, and it
            names the thing behind every point the way the Attributes row
            does. --}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.Bonuses"}}</h4>
      <dl class="azeroth-force-list">
        {{#each overview.inForce.scalars as |row|}}
        <dt>{{localize row.label}}</dt>
        <dd><span class="azeroth-force-value">+{{row.points}}</span> <span class="azeroth-force-from">{{row.from}}</span></dd>
        {{/each}}
      </dl>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if overview.inForce.fortitude}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.Fortitude"}}</h4>
      <p class="azeroth-force-line">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.FortitudeHealth" n=overview.inForce.fortitude}}</p>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if overview.inForce.signatures.length}}
      {{!-- What the Signatures on what is WORN are doing (08 SS20, S3; D-692):
            the item, what kind of Signature it carries, whether its gate holds
            for this bearer, and a Use button where there is one to press. A
            standing Signature draws as text with no button anywhere (D-681),
            and a gate that fails is said in words rather than by a grey. --}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Signature.Heading"}}</h4>
      <ul class="azeroth-force-signatures">
        {{#each overview.inForce.signatures as |s|}}
        {{!-- A ROW'S TEXT FLOOR IS 13px, not the column's 12 (D-608): every
              one of these lines is inside a list item, so `.azeroth-force-from`
              beside them would measure `small` on every one. --}}
        <li data-item-id="{{s.id}}">
          <span class="azeroth-force-signature-name{{#if s.rarityClass}} {{s.rarityClass}}{{/if}}"
                data-action="openItem" role="button" tabindex="0">{{s.name}}</span>
          {{#if s.kindLabel}}<span class="azeroth-force-signature-note">{{localize s.kindLabel}}</span>{{/if}}
          {{#if s.pressable}}
          <button type="button" class="azeroth-use" data-action="useSignature"{{#if s.refusal}} disabled{{/if}}>{{localize "AZEROTH.Feature.Use"}}</button>
          {{/if}}
          {{#if s.gateFails}}<span class="azeroth-force-signature-note">{{localize "AZEROTH.Signature.GateFails"}}</span>{{/if}}
          {{!-- A GATE COVERS ONLY ITS OWN SENTENCE (D-722). This column is a
                SUMMARY, so it names each gated sentence's gate and leaves the
                holds/fails sentence to the Combat panel and the item sheet -
                without the line a Signature half of which is a Shaman's reads
                here as ungated. --}}
          {{#each s.gatedParts as |part|}}
          <span class="azeroth-force-signature-note">{{localize "AZEROTH.Signature.PartOnly"}} {{#each part.gates as |g|}}{{#unless @first}} · {{/unless}}{{#if g.value}}{{localize "AZEROTH.Signature.GateValue" kind=(localize g.label) value=g.value}}{{else}}{{localize g.label}}{{/if}}{{/each}}</span>
          {{/each}}
          {{#if s.refusalLabel}}<span class="azeroth-force-signature-note">{{localize s.refusalLabel}}</span>{{/if}}
        </li>
        {{/each}}
      </ul>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if overview.inForce.augment}}
      {{!-- 07 SS3: the Augment reaches the Casting Test and nothing else, so
            the line says what it does rather than printing a bare number. --}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.Casting"}}</h4>
      <p class="azeroth-force-line">{{localize "AZEROTH.Augment.HeldNote" name=overview.inForce.augment.name}}</p>
      <p class="azeroth-force-line"><span class="azeroth-force-value">+{{overview.inForce.augment.bonus}}</span>
        <span class="azeroth-force-from">{{localize "AZEROTH.Overview.CastingTest"}}</span></p>
      {{/if}}

      {{!-- A heading and the number, never the word twice: the heading IS the
            term here, and printing both read as a stutter in the shot. --}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.Defense"}}</h4>
      <p class="azeroth-force-line"><span class="azeroth-force-value">{{azerothDash overview.inForce.defense}}</span></p>

      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.ArmorPoints"}}</h4>
      <dl class="azeroth-force-list">
        {{#each overview.inForce.ap as |row|}}
        <dt>{{localize row.label}}</dt>
        <dd><span class="azeroth-force-value">{{row.value}}</span></dd>
        {{/each}}
      </dl>

      {{!-- The same carry line the Gear tab's head prints, from the same
            object (05 *Speed and movement*, 08 SS11; D-735): bag slots, with
            the state in words beside the numbers and the overflow said in
            words where there is any. --}}
      <h4 class="azeroth-overview-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.CarryCapacity"}}</h4>
      <p class="azeroth-force-line">
        {{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.BagSlotsOf" used=overview.inForce.load.carried max=overview.inForce.load.capacity}}
        <span class="azeroth-force-from">{{localize overview.inForce.load.label}}</span>
        {{#if overview.inForce.load.over}}<span class="azeroth-force-from">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.BagSlotsOver" n=overview.inForce.load.over}}</span>{{/if}}
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
